+Aegis Automation Sprint Plan — Goal: raise automation from ~51% → ~75% (12 week roadmap)
+
+Overview
+- Objective: Automate high-impact manual operations while preserving human-in-the-loop for custody/legal/audit actions.
+- Duration: 12 weeks (3 two-week sprints + stabilization)
+- Outcome: scripted HSM rotation workflows with safe operator confirmations, hardware runner bootstrap automation, active-learning labeling loop to reduce labeling labor, and repo automation inventory with CI reporting.
+
+Sprint 0 (Weeks 0-2) — Safety & Scaffolding (blockers)
+- Tasks:
+  1) Review & sign policies for automation (Legal & Crypto) — Owner: Legal/Crypto — 2 days
+  2) Deploy inventory CI and run baseline report (tools/inventory_automation.py + workflow) — Owner: Platform — 1 day
+  3) Install operator toolset on bastion (aws, vault, cosign, jq, python) — Owner: Platform — 1 day
+  4) Review kill-switch & delegation enforcer integration with orchestrator — Owner: Platform/Crypto — 2 days
+- Success criteria: baseline inventory report produced; kill-switch read/write validated in staging
+
+Sprint 1 (Weeks 3-4) — HSM Rotation Automation & Safer Sign/Promote
+- Tasks:
+  1) Implement safe orchestration script for rotation (ops/hsm/auto_rotate_workflow.py) — Owner: Crypto/Platform — 3 days
+  2) Add guard rails: operator confirmation prompts, auditing of each step to Vault, optional dry-run mode — Owner: Crypto — 2 days
+  3) Test rotation script on staging artifacts (dry run) and assert re-sign flows (rotate_and_resign.py) — Owner: Platform — 2 days
+  4) Document runbook for rotation drill (docs/runbooks) — Owner: Crypto — 1 day
+- Success criteria: rotation script runs in dry-run; re-sign flow validated against sample artifact list; audit manifests written to evidence bucket
+
+Sprint 2 (Weeks 5-7) — Hardware/Runner Bootstrap & CI Integration
+- Tasks:
+  1) Create runner bootstrap script & cloud-init for GPU/TPU/Neuron (ops/hardware/bootstrap_runner.sh + cloud-init) — Owner: Platform — 3 days
+  2) Automate runner registration & hardware diagnostics (deploy/selfhosted runner diag integration) — Owner: Platform/ML Eng — 3 days
+  3) End-to-end validation: register one runner, run runner_hw_diagnostics.py and CI job — Owner: ML Eng — 3 days
+- Success criteria: one validated self-hosted runner that passes diagnostics and completes a sample MLflow job
+
+Sprint 3 (Weeks 8-10) — Active Learning Labeling Pipeline
+- Tasks:
+  1) Implement active-learning loop that selects high-uncertainty examples (services/labeling/active_learning_loop.py) — Owner: ML Eng / Safety — 3 days
+  2) Integrate labeling task writer (CSV/GCS/S3 + optional GitHub issue creation) — Owner: ML Eng — 2 days
+  3) Run pilot labeling campaign (2–5k items) and retrain calibrator; validate threshold improvements — Owner: Safety/ML Eng — 5 days
+- Success criteria: labeling throughput increased (target 2–5k), calibrator precision improved and threshold persisted to Vault
+
+Sprint 4 (Weeks 11-12) — Stabilize, Audit & Handover
+- Tasks:
+  1) Run 1 full rotation drill including auditor signoff (manual step but scripted) — Owner: Crypto/Auditor — 2 days
+  2) Finalize runbooks, training, and automated alerts for script failures — Owner: Platform/SRE — 3 days
+  3) Hand over runbooks and provide operator training session — Owner: Platform/Crypto — 1 day
+- Success criteria: rotation drill logged in evidence bucket & Vault, operator signoff, runbooks accepted by auditors
+
+KPIs & Acceptance Criteria
+- Automated rotation run time (dry-run) < 30 minutes (excluding manual approvals)
+- Runner bootstrap reproducibility: a new runner passes diagnostics in < 60 minutes (post-procurement)
+- Labeling throughput: at least 100 labeled examples/day per labeling team member with active-learning assistance
+- Calibrator precision: >= target (e.g., 0.90) on holdout after retrain
+- Inventory automation coverage: > 90% of repo actionable items classified
+
+Risk & Mitigations
+- Risk: Automating key/custody steps prematurely — Mitigation: require auditor signoff and operator confirmations; dry-run first
+- Risk: Hardware driver installation variability — Mitigation: create per-vendor documented install steps and CI hardware diagnostic checks
+- Risk: Label noise harming calibrator — Mitigation: implement label QA & consensus aggregation; sample adjudication
+
+Notes
+- This plan assumes you accept operator involvement for custody/auditor steps. Removing humans entirely for high-risk actions requires insurer/legal signoff and additional verification features (beyond this plan).
+
